($t$Fagraea fragrans$t$, $t$Fagraea fragrans$t$, $t$Gentianaceae$t$, $t$Famiglia botanica: Gentianaceae. Portamento: Tree. Altezza massima indicativa: 25 m. Fagraea fragrans or commonly known as Ironwood or Tembusu is a large evergreen tree native to Southeast Asia. The trunk is dark brown and deeply fissured. The leaves are oval and light green in colour. The flowers are yellowish with distinct fragrance. The fruits are bitter, red berries. Ironwood grows up to 25 m tall with a straight, cylindrical bole of up to 150 cm in diameter. It yields a high quality timber, and an excellent fuel and charcoal. When established, it is moderately tolerant to drought. Bark decoction is used as a febrifuge to treat conditions such as malaria. On the other hand, decoction of twigs and leaves is used for dysentery and severe diarrhoea. The skin of the fruits yields latex which can be used as an adhesive. The wood is used for posts and piles, bridges and ships, chopping blocks, furniture, cabinet work, etc.$t$, $j${"luce": "Pieno sole", "acqua": "Abbondante, terreno costantemente umido", "terreno": "Tollera terreno: sabbioso/leggero, medio, argilloso/pesante"}$j$::jsonb, ARRAY[$t$Scheda in bozza, importata automaticamente da Plants For A Future (pfaf.org): dati non verificati manualmente, da controllare prima di considerarli affidabili$t$, $t$Nome comune (inglese, fonte PFAF): Ironwood, Tembusu$t$, $t$Rischi segnalati dalla fonte (testo originale in inglese, non tradotto per non alterarne il significato): Skin rashes may develop when handling green logs with bark on[ 316 ].$t$], $j${"irrigazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "concimazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "potatura": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "npk": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}}$j$::jsonb, $j${"famiglia_botanica": "Gentianaceae", "giorni_germinazione